  "summary": "The clean-cut modernist youth culture of tailored Italian suits, parkas, scooters and R&B, all-night dancing and sharp detail.",
  "description": "Working-class London \"modernists\" spent wages on fine tailoring, Fred Perry polos, levis, US army fishtail parkas and Lambretta/Vespa scooters, dancing to R&B, bluebeat and Motown at all-nighters. The 1964 seaside battles and The Who's Quadrophenia mythologized the scene. Mod's sharpness fed skinhead, northern soul, scooterboy and Britpop revivals; it remains the template of subcultural dandyism.",
